title: "Bubble and particle collision: flow around a rising bubble, collision efficiency, synthetic PIV and turbulence around bubbles"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ishaque
    given-names: Hashim
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-20
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/hashimishaque-platform/bubble-particle-collision"
url: "https://hashimishaque.com/bubble-particle-collision/"
keywords:
  - flotation
  - bubble-particle collision
  - collision efficiency
  - Navier-Stokes
  - lattice Boltzmann
  - Maxey-Riley
  - particle image velocimetry
  - turbulence
abstract: >-
  A browser program, with a command-line interface, for the flow around a rising bubble and
  the collision of particles with it, as in flotation. It solves the axisymmetric Navier-Stokes
  equations around the bubble, follows particles with the Maxey-Riley equation, computes the
  collision efficiency, makes and evaluates synthetic PIV recordings, draws bubble swarms with
  synthetic turbulence, and runs a live two-dimensional lattice Boltzmann simulation of a bubble
  in a turbulent stream. Every part is checked against exact solutions or published values.
